WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.901 --> 00:00:02.300
-You've been so great to me.

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:04.300
You've Zoomed into the show
a bunch of times to help me out.

00:00:04.300 --> 00:00:06.033
And I really appreciate it.
Thank you so much.

00:00:06.033 --> 00:00:07.634
To see you in person,
it makes me so happy.

00:00:07.634 --> 00:00:09.067
-Thank you.

00:00:09.067 --> 00:00:11.434
You've been there for me since
the beginning of my career.

00:00:11.434 --> 00:00:13.000
-No, is that true?

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:15.367
When was that? Awhile.
-Yes, for a long time.

00:00:15.367 --> 00:00:16.701
-You just recently
celebrated your birthday.

00:00:16.701 --> 00:00:18.834
-I did. My 25th birthday.

00:00:18.834 --> 00:00:20.133
-Thank you.

00:00:20.133 --> 00:00:22.868
-Happy 25th, of course!
-Thank you. Thank you.

00:00:22.868 --> 00:00:25.133
-You had a surprise party,
is what I heard.

00:00:25.133 --> 00:00:26.934
-I did.
Do you like surprise parties?

00:00:26.934 --> 00:00:28.634
-Did you enjoy it?
-I love surprise parties.

00:00:28.634 --> 00:00:30.934
It's just really hard
to surprise me.

00:00:30.934 --> 00:00:32.534
-It is?
-Yeah, I'm a Virgo, and...

00:00:32.534 --> 00:00:33.701
-[ Gasps ] Me, too!

00:00:33.701 --> 00:00:34.901
[ Cheering ]

00:00:34.901 --> 00:00:37.267
-Hey, that's why we --
See? Oh, look at that.

00:00:37.267 --> 00:00:38.701
-Wow.
-Twins.

00:00:38.701 --> 00:00:40.634
[ Laughter ]

00:00:40.634 --> 00:00:42.734
We'll be like why couldn't we --

00:00:42.734 --> 00:00:44.067
[ Laughing ]

00:00:44.067 --> 00:00:45.200
Virgos.

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:47.300
But, I, it is...

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:48.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:52.200
It is very hard to surprise me,
because I am very nosy

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:53.601
and I can hear a pin drop.

00:00:53.601 --> 00:00:55.100
-Yeah, you can.
-So I can literally,

00:00:55.100 --> 00:00:57.100
I can hear my assistant
in the back right now,

00:00:57.100 --> 00:00:58.133
while I'm talking to you.

00:00:58.133 --> 00:00:59.634
-Yeah?
-I can hear her.

00:00:59.634 --> 00:01:01.200
-So how did they do it?

00:01:01.200 --> 00:01:03.501
-I was very busy.
It was Fashion Week.

00:01:03.501 --> 00:01:08.334
So I had a huge, big schedule,
and they threw in some fitting,

00:01:08.334 --> 00:01:10.734
some random fitting,
and I was upset about it,

00:01:10.734 --> 00:01:13.801
because I was like,
"Who has a fitting at 7:00 PM?"

00:01:13.801 --> 00:01:14.968
-Yeah.
-You know?

00:01:14.968 --> 00:01:16.767
And so I was like,
"I'm going to wear this."

00:01:16.767 --> 00:01:18.000
And she was like, "No!

00:01:18.000 --> 00:01:19.667
You have to wear the dress
that your stylist sent!"

00:01:19.667 --> 00:01:21.133
And I was like,
"What? It's a fitting!"

00:01:21.133 --> 00:01:23.534
So I cooperated,
and I'm glad I did,

00:01:23.534 --> 00:01:25.267
'cause they got me.

00:01:25.267 --> 00:01:26.734
They got me good.

00:01:26.734 --> 00:01:29.801
-So you go into this thing.
Were you in a bad mood?

00:01:29.801 --> 00:01:32.033
-I was a little sour,

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:35.534
because I'm going to wardrobe
fitting at 7:00 PM.

00:01:35.534 --> 00:01:36.834
Like, y'all couldn't
do this earlier?

00:01:36.834 --> 00:01:38.167
-Yeah, and then you walk in...

00:01:38.167 --> 00:01:39.467
-And I walk and they're like,
"Surprise!"

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:42.000
And I was like --
rr, eeh, ahh!

00:01:42.000 --> 00:01:43.601
Like, I was...

00:01:43.601 --> 00:01:45.133
-You had real heavy emotions.
-I was happy. Yeah.

00:01:45.133 --> 00:01:47.901
I was happy but I was mad,
'cause they got me.

00:01:47.901 --> 00:01:49.067
-But you said,
happy to see everybody.

00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:50.601
Well, happy, happy birthday.
-Thank you.

00:01:50.601 --> 00:01:52.200
-You look gorgeous tonight.

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.534
-Thank you.
Say it again. What else?

00:01:53.534 --> 00:01:56.167
-You always look gorgeous.
-Oh.

00:01:56.167 --> 00:01:58.133
-This is you
at the Met Gala, by the way.

00:01:58.133 --> 00:02:00.400
Look at this. Fantastic.
-Oh, that was amazing.

00:02:00.400 --> 00:02:02.934
-Look at this, now. Come on.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:02.934 --> 00:02:04.868
-Everyone was
talking about this.

00:02:04.868 --> 00:02:06.801
-Were they?
-Oh, yeah. Are you kidding me?

00:02:06.801 --> 00:02:09.300
You were in all the fashion
magazines, you had the papers.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.868
-Really?
-Yeah.

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:12.534
-I don't pay attention
to that stuff

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:13.834
'cause I don't want
my feelings hurt,

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:15.767
so I just take the picture
and I never look back.

00:02:15.767 --> 00:02:16.868
-Oh, no,
these were all great stuff.

00:02:16.868 --> 00:02:18.067
-Okay, good.

00:02:18.067 --> 00:02:20.267
-What was the theme this year
at the Gala?

00:02:20.267 --> 00:02:23.467
-It was Hollywood Glamour.
Old Hollywood glamour.

00:02:23.467 --> 00:02:25.667
I just decided
to tap into Diana Ross,

00:02:25.667 --> 00:02:27.200
because I just love her so much.

00:02:27.200 --> 00:02:30.100
-I love Diana Ross.
-She embodies glamour.

00:02:30.100 --> 00:02:31.434
-Come on. Right?
-Yeah.

00:02:31.434 --> 00:02:33.200
-That Central Park show
is the one I always think about.

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:35.000
The wind, and the yeah,
and it was raining.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:37.200
Oh, she's unbelievable.
-Class act.

00:02:37.200 --> 00:02:39.767
-There's so many famous people
you meet at the Gala.

00:02:39.767 --> 00:02:42.300
Who'd you hang with?

00:02:42.300 --> 00:02:44.033
-Well, you know I saw Mary,
so...

00:02:44.033 --> 00:02:45.234
-[ Gasps ] I love Mary J. Blige.

00:02:45.234 --> 00:02:47.601
-That's my bestest friend
in the industry, yes.

00:02:47.601 --> 00:02:51.801
-I love Mary.
-And so I saw her,

00:02:51.801 --> 00:02:53.901
and then we ran into
Meg Thee Stallion.

00:02:53.901 --> 00:02:56.167
-[ Gasps ] My other...

00:02:56.167 --> 00:02:57.701
-Y'all know that's my baby girl.

00:02:57.701 --> 00:02:59.801
She put me in her video,
"Body-ody-ody."

00:02:59.801 --> 00:03:03.000
-That's right, she did.
-She's the best.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.734
She's funny.
-And then she was intrigued

00:03:05.734 --> 00:03:07.534
with the...

00:03:07.534 --> 00:03:09.033
Well, there was certain
parts of our bodies

00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:10.667
that was showing in our...

00:03:10.667 --> 00:03:13.067
Well, okay, so mine,
in the back,

00:03:13.067 --> 00:03:16.400
it had a dip in the back,
as well, and so I had --

00:03:16.400 --> 00:03:18.367
-Deeper than this dip?
-See that dip, there?

00:03:18.367 --> 00:03:19.968
-Yes.
-It was in the back as well.

00:03:19.968 --> 00:03:24.133
So it was like,
a little, sexy plumber's crack.

00:03:24.133 --> 00:03:25.767
[ Laughter ]

00:03:25.767 --> 00:03:28.767
And then Mary's dress
was kind of revealing, too.

00:03:28.767 --> 00:03:30.200
-Sexy plumber's crack?

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:31.567
-Yeah.
-That's so funny.

00:03:31.567 --> 00:03:33.934
-So what she did is she posts,
she put us on her Story

00:03:33.934 --> 00:03:37.467
and she was like, "Ooh,
that sexy butt crack."

00:03:37.467 --> 00:03:41.300
-Are you recording
anything with Megan?

00:03:41.300 --> 00:03:43.567
Ahh
-Ooh. What did you hear?

00:03:43.567 --> 00:03:45.167
-Well, I don't know.
I know that you can sing.

00:03:45.167 --> 00:03:46.501
And I heard that you actually

00:03:46.501 --> 00:03:48.167
were working on
a little EP or something.

00:03:48.167 --> 00:03:50.100
-It's crazy,
because it found me.

00:03:50.100 --> 00:03:52.000
Like, I didn't go seeking it.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:55.601
I was looking for a song
for one thing that I was doing,

00:03:55.601 --> 00:03:58.901
and so I reached out
to some producer friends I know,

00:03:58.901 --> 00:04:01.300
and then they sent me these
incredible beats and I was like,

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:03.300
"Well, how do I pick one?

00:04:03.300 --> 00:04:04.934
I'll just do an EP."

00:04:04.934 --> 00:04:06.400
-Do all of them.
Look at you.

00:04:06.400 --> 00:04:09.601
-But I'm telling you, listen,
I was not looking for music.

00:04:09.601 --> 00:04:11.100
It found me --
first in "The Muppets" --

00:04:11.100 --> 00:04:12.901
if you saw the
"Muppets Haunted Mansion,"

00:04:12.901 --> 00:04:14.267
I sang in that.

00:04:14.267 --> 00:04:16.133
And then the next thing,
Miss Hannigan.

00:04:16.133 --> 00:04:18.501
There's something else
I'm being tapped for right now,

00:04:18.501 --> 00:04:22.167
but I can't say anything
until the ink dries.

00:04:22.167 --> 00:04:23.968
-Wow, really?
-And it really involves music.

00:04:23.968 --> 00:04:25.133
-[ Gasps ]
-And then my EP.

00:04:25.133 --> 00:04:28.067
It's just like,
"What are you doing?"

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:30.300
-I'm so happy for you, though,
because I know you can do it.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:31.601
Do you know when it's going
to come out or no?

00:04:31.601 --> 00:04:33.601
-Top of the year. Stay tuned.
-Okay. Alright.

00:04:33.601 --> 00:04:34.834
January. Taraji P. Henson.

00:04:34.834 --> 00:04:36.701
I'm just saying,
look out for something good.

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:38.267
I'm talking about "Annie"
right now.

00:04:38.267 --> 00:04:40.300
-Okay.
-This is Miss Hannigan.

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:41.968
Look at you.

00:04:41.968 --> 00:04:43.734
[ Applause ]

00:04:43.734 --> 00:04:44.968
Come on.

00:04:44.968 --> 00:04:47.767
So, wait, how's it going?
-So much fun.

00:04:47.767 --> 00:04:50.868
-Great cast.
-Great. I mean, dynamic.

00:04:50.868 --> 00:04:52.667
Just wait until
you see these little --

00:04:52.667 --> 00:04:54.934
I call them my biscuits
and my little cookies

00:04:54.934 --> 00:04:56.434
and my little ladybugs.

00:04:56.434 --> 00:04:58.167
-Yeah.
-The little orphans.

00:04:58.167 --> 00:04:59.501
Oh, my God. They're so amazing.

00:04:59.501 --> 00:05:02.767
And Celina is going to
blow you away, our Annie.

00:05:02.767 --> 00:05:05.601
-Really?
-Harry is a pain in my butt.

00:05:05.601 --> 00:05:09.267
-Harry Connick Jr.?
-No, I love him. He's amazing.

00:05:09.267 --> 00:05:12.801
He has this Southern drawl
that just, you're like,

00:05:12.801 --> 00:05:15.000
"Say something again, Harry."

00:05:15.000 --> 00:05:16.534
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Exactly, right?

00:05:16.534 --> 00:05:18.667
Oh, I love him so much.
-He's so incredible.

00:05:18.667 --> 00:05:21.701
-But the book,
the music on this is just...

00:05:21.701 --> 00:05:23.934
-You know what's
amazing about this play?

00:05:23.934 --> 00:05:25.934
The subject matter.

00:05:25.934 --> 00:05:28.067
They're talking about
the Great Depression

00:05:28.067 --> 00:05:30.167
and Broadway opening back up.

00:05:30.167 --> 00:05:31.901
Does that sound familiar
to you guys?

00:05:31.901 --> 00:05:33.934
-Yeah, it's eerie, right?

00:05:33.934 --> 00:05:36.567
-It's very eerie.
-Yeah.

00:05:36.567 --> 00:05:38.801
What is your big number?

00:05:38.801 --> 00:05:42.234
-Oh, I have "Little Girls."
I have "Sign." "Easy Street."

00:05:42.234 --> 00:05:43.367
-Oh, my God.

00:05:43.367 --> 00:05:46.467
-Oh, and "Sign" is
with Harry Connick and I.

00:05:46.467 --> 00:05:48.033
That's our duet.
-Okay.

00:05:48.033 --> 00:05:52.234
-And then I have "Little Girls."

00:05:52.234 --> 00:05:55.167
That's Miss Hannigan's solo.

00:05:55.167 --> 00:05:56.701
And then we have "Easy Street."

00:05:56.701 --> 00:05:58.400
-This thing is live.
-It's live.

00:05:58.400 --> 00:06:00.133
-Are you nervous at all?
-Of course.

00:06:00.133 --> 00:06:02.133
Nerves are good, though.
-Yeah, they are.

00:06:02.133 --> 00:06:04.834
-If you're not nervous,
I'm concerned.

00:06:04.834 --> 00:06:08.200
Nerves means you're alive.
You're in the moment.

00:06:08.200 --> 00:06:09.901
You're right here in the moment.

00:06:09.901 --> 00:06:11.701
-Yes!
-They're to be used.

00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:12.968
-That's exactly right.
-Absolutely.

00:06:12.968 --> 00:06:15.033
-I cannot wait for
this performance

00:06:15.033 --> 00:06:16.067
and I love you so much.

00:06:16.067 --> 00:06:17.400
We're doing more
with Taraji P. Henson.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:18.634
Come back.
More "Tonight Show," everybody.

